Description:
Nigeria, medium group of Mumuye adult males walking along road. Males wearing "goat-skin" aprons, some carrying sticks and bundles. Savanna setting, mountains in background.
Medium:  
Gelatin silver print.;

Nigeria, adult female carrying pile of pots and baskets in frame [?] on head. Female wearing waist-ornament, arm-ornament. Section-view of similar female at right. Dry rural setting, small herd of goats or cattle in background.
Medium:  
Gelatin silver print.;

Photograph (black and white), view of six European men, four sitting on chairs and two standing. Man sitting at left wearing gaiters and holding riding-crop. Behind the group are two horses attended by two men (one almost occluded).  Domestic dog with fore legs up is in front of the men
Albumen print.
Format: Section of print missing at bottom right.;

Nigeria [?], two halves of a large fruit, displayed on rocking-chair with scale. Indoor setting.
Medium: Albumen print [?].
Format: Vignette.;

Study of medium group of objects from Lagos. Each appears to be made of a number of objects together on string. Plain backdrop.
Medium: Gelatin silver print.
Format: Mounted on card. Image very dark.;

Nigeria, adult female carrying pile of pots and baskets in frame [?] on head. Female wearing waist-ornament, arm-ornaments. Section-view of similar female at left. Savanna setting, herd of goats or cattle in background.
Medium:  
Gelatin silver print.;

Nigeria, two adult females standing on path outdoors. Carrying bundles of leaves on heads. Females wearing bundles of leaves hanging from waist-bands, carrying sticks. Savanna setting.
Medium:  
Gelatin silver print.;

Street of colonial-style buildings along waterfront. Male and female adults, wearing European clothing, walking along street. Sign saying "ELDER DEMPSTER AND COMPANY LTD" on front of one building. Several rowing boats moored beside slipway. Adults in Euro-American dress beside boats. Warehouse [?] and market [?] on waterfront.
Medium: Black and white. Gelatin silver print [?].
Prior to being stored in albums AF/48, AF/49 and AF/50, the loose photographs and postcards donated by Lady Menendez were kept in boxes and envelopes.;

Inscription:
Inscription type: annotation Inscription quoted: Album Title: "1st BENIN. WARRI. & SAPELE. 2nd NEW CALABAR. BONNY. OPOBO & QUA COUNTRY." [manuscript note on album paper].
Original Description: "Chief Wilbraid & his Soldiers Bakana New Calabar"
[manuscript note on album paper]; "J. A. Green, Artist Photographer Bonny, Opobo, &c., &c." [stamp on back of print].;

Description:
Nigeria [?], portrait of medium group of adult male polo players, Europeans and two Africans. Males mounted on horses in field.
Medium: Albumen print (?).
Format: Print cut in oval shape.;

Picture of the Igbo maiden mask called AGBHOGHO MMANWU.  With elaborate hair-style or head-dress with spiral patterns. Appears to be made of carved and painted wood.
Plain backdrop.
Medium: Gelatin silver print.;

Picture of nine men. Four Europeans sitting and five Africans standing. The man sitting at right in military uniform.
Medium: Black and white. Gelatin silver print (?).
Format: Print mounted on gilt-edged card.;

Inscription:
Inscription type: annotation Inscription quoted: Original Number: "A" [manuscript note on back of print]; "88" [manuscript note on card accompanying photograph].
