Description:
Photograph (black and white); view of a polo team. Eight adult males on horse-back holding polo sticks, one adult male standing in the middle of the group. Males wearing American dress.
Vignette image. Lagos, Nigeria
Gelatin silver print;

Picture of a group of people sitting in a courtroom. Two uniformed Africans sitting behind a table. Europeans behind Africans.  Two banners bearing Union Jack flags and saying "NEW PROVIDENCE ... OLD CALABAR" on wall behind dock. British coat of arms, between flags.
Medium: Black and white.
Format: Photograph is mounted on card with rounded corners and gilt edges.;

Oshe Shango baton (with four carved faces) made of wood, metal, beads.
Register 1954
Carved wood baton with forked top, two pairs of faces with metal eye pupils: two strings of red and pink beads wound round the handle.;

Picture of three men. One on horse back, the others beside the horse. Wearing northern Nigerian attire. Horse wearing ornate harness.
Medium: Black and white.
Format: Photograph is mounted on card with rounded corners and gilt edges.;

Photograph (black and white); view of two dug-out canoes, each paddled by a young adult using Niger Delta paddles. Nigeria
Printed ephemera
Gelatin silver print;

